EXECUTIVE DELTA

The highest-information-gain discovery this run is a new regulatory
frontier outside the earlier DWT/grid watchlist: the EU Data Act
Article 3(1) design obligation became applicable on 12 September 2026
to connected products and related services placed on the EU market
after that date. The legal text requires product/service data and
relevant metadata to be available to the user easily, securely, free
of charge, in a comprehensive, structured, commonly used and
machine-readable format and, where relevant/technically feasible,
directly accessible. The Act explicitly encompasses hardware status
and malfunction data. CONFIRMED.

This is unusually aligned with POW
repair/property/robotics/vehicle/industrial-equipment branches because
it creates NEW user-accessible machine state prospectively by product
cohort. It is not a single public feed: access is
product/user-specific, so the legitimate POW route is first-party
consenting users/businesses and manufacturer-supported exports/APIs.
Promote to P0 WATCH + PILOT DISCOVERY, not PLANT, until executable
vendor interfaces are identified.

The existing #1 near-term UK feed remains DEFRA Digital Waste
Tracking. Mandatory receiver reporting starts 1 Oct 2026 in
England/Wales; Phase 2 Collections has passed Alpha and is targeting
private beta in autumn 2026. The critical action remains preserving
receipt identity now and watching official code/schema for the first
Collections API artifact.

