NEW FRONTIER: EU DATA ACT CONNECTED-PRODUCT STATE

Exact legal trigger: Regulation (EU) 2023/2854 Article 50 says Article
3(1)'s obligation applies to connected products and related services
placed on the market after 12 September 2026. Article 3 requires
machine-readable user access by design. The legal recitals expressly
include sensor data, hardware status, malfunctions and even changing
battery/component state while products are idle. CONFIRMED.

What genuinely begins now: a new cohort of connected physical products
for which user-accessible structured machine data is a design
obligation. This is not merely an API wrapper over an old government
database. The underlying product telemetry may have existed internally
before, but the user's structured access right/design obligation for
newly placed products begins with this cohort. CONFIRMED.

POW opportunity: create a vendor/interface registry keyed by
manufacturer + product family + model + market-placement cohort,
recording the actual supported access mechanism (direct device,
documented API, export, related-service endpoint), fields, sampling
cadence, retention, authentication and third-party sharing path. Then,
with explicit user/business consent, normalize product telemetry into
POW's physical state ontology.

Candidate new events: COMPONENT_HEALTH_CHANGED, FAULT_REPORTED,
BATTERY_STATE_CHANGED, CONSUMPTION_CHANGED, OPERATING_MODE_CHANGED,
SERVICE_REQUIRED, FIRMWARE_CHANGED, PERFORMANCE_DEGRADED.

Canonical identity: manufacturer + model/family + manufacturer
serial/device ID where supplied; never infer serials. Preserve
product-placement/manufacture evidence separately because the 12-Sep
cohort boundary matters.

